1
00:00:42,430 --> 00:00:43,770
It's almost morning.

2
00:00:43,770 --> 00:00:45,450
We should've found a town by now.

3
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:48,060
This is the way the woodsman told us to go, right?

4
00:00:48,730 --> 00:00:51,070
Have you listened to anything I've been saying?

5
00:00:51,070 --> 00:00:53,680
For the last couple hours, I've been saying...

6
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:56,740
Well, that settles it.

7
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:58,690
I'm gonna walk up ten feet ahead of you.

8
00:00:58,690 --> 00:01:00,030
- Help!
- Huh?

9
00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:00,930
I'm stuck!

10
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:02,040
I hear something!

11
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:03,540
It's probably nothing.

12
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:04,710
Hey, look.

13
00:01:04,710 --> 00:01:06,960
"Pottsfield, 1 mile."

14
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:08,960
A town! Let's go this way.

15
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,960
Okay, let's go this way.

16
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,880
Not... ugh.

17
00:01:13,150 --> 00:01:13,880
Hello?

18
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:15,340
Hello?

19
00:01:15,340 --> 00:01:16,880
- Hey, you.
- Who? Me?

20
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:18,390
- Yeah, you.
- Oh.

21
00:01:18,390 --> 00:01:19,390
Hello.

22
00:01:19,390 --> 00:01:21,390
It's you again. I'm stuck.

23
00:01:21,390 --> 00:01:23,220
Help me out of here, and I'll owe you a favor.

24
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:25,060
Whoa! I get a wish?

25
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:26,490
No, no, no. Not a wish.

26
00:01:26,490 --> 00:01:27,430
I'm not magical.

27
00:01:27,430 --> 00:01:28,810
I'll just do you a good turn.

28
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:30,820
Can you turn me into a tiger?

29
00:01:30,820 --> 00:01:33,900
Um, no. I just said I'm not magical.

30
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:35,900
It doesn't have to be a magical tiger.

31
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:38,210
Greg, stop talking to a bush.

32
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:39,700
- Okay.
- Huh?

33
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:41,160
Thanks. I owe you a favor.

34
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:42,450
So, um...

35
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:44,700
you two are lost kids with no purpose in life, right?

36
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:45,540
Uh-huh.

37
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:49,460
How about I bring you to Adelaide of the pasture,

38
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:51,590
the good woman of the woods?

39
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:53,590
She could help you get home.

40
00:01:53,590 --> 00:01:54,550
Oh.

41
00:01:54,550 --> 00:01:56,210
N-No, no. No, no.

42
00:01:56,210 --> 00:01:57,190
No, no, no, no, no, no.

43
00:01:57,190 --> 00:01:59,920
Magic talking birds leading us to fairy godmothers

44
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:01,550
in the mysterious...

45
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:03,260
I'm going to Pottsfield.

46
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:04,980
Yeah, we're going to Pottsfield.

47
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:05,720
Come on!

48
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:06,760
What about the favor?

49
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,720
I'll think of my wish later.

50
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:09,810
Ohh.

51
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:18,570
So, let's small-talk.

52
00:02:18,570 --> 00:02:20,450
My name's Greg. What's yours?

53
00:02:20,450 --> 00:02:21,140
Beatrice.

54
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:22,930
My brother's name is Wirt.

55
00:02:22,930 --> 00:02:23,620
Who cares?

56
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:27,160
And my frog's name is Wirt Jr.

57
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:28,340
but that may change.

58
00:02:28,340 --> 00:02:29,440
Okay, that's great.

59
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:31,870
How about you and I ditch your brother?

60
00:02:31,870 --> 00:02:33,380
Mm. Maybe later.

61
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:34,910
So, is it nice being a bird?

62
00:02:34,910 --> 00:02:36,390
- Nope.
- Oh.

63
00:02:36,390 --> 00:02:37,770
Do you like waffles?

64
00:02:37,770 --> 00:02:39,490
No, waffles make me sick.

65
00:02:39,490 --> 00:02:41,380
I eat... m-maggots.

66
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:42,720
- Ahh!
- What?!

67
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:44,320
How can you not eat waffles?!

68
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:45,720
- Ahh!
- What?

69
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:47,020
I stepped on a pumpkin!

70
00:02:47,020 --> 00:02:47,890
Aha!

71
00:02:48,390 --> 00:02:50,340
Civilization, see?

72
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:50,900
Now...

73
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:51,850
Huh? What the...

74
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:56,690
All right. Let's rejoin society.

75
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:05,280
Hello? Hello?

76
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:06,290
Hm,

77
00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:07,730
see anybody?

78
00:03:07,730 --> 00:03:09,290
No...

79
00:03:09,370 --> 00:03:11,020
Oh, I see you.

80
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:12,560
Yeah, I see you, too, Greg.

81
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:15,110
Hey, not to be obnoxious, but an abandoned ghost town

82
00:03:15,110 --> 00:03:18,290
doesn't seem like it's gonna be that useful getting you guys home.

83
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:20,720
There's got to be somebody...

84
00:03:21,050 --> 00:03:22,300
somewhere.

85
00:03:22,930 --> 00:03:23,800
Excuse me?

86
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:25,520
Anyone here?

87
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:27,310
Hello?

88
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,350
Oh. Sorry.

89
00:03:29,350 --> 00:03:30,260
Uh,

90
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:32,810
I'm looking for a phone.

91
00:03:32,810 --> 00:03:34,560
Um, I'm sorry.

92
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:37,640
Did you find anything?

93
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:39,000
Nope. Where's Greg?

94
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,280
Do you hear that?

95
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:40,990
Huh?

96
00:03:40,990 --> 00:03:43,200
♪ ...let spirits meet ♪

97
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:47,410
♪ around the barn of Pottsfield town ♪

98
00:03:46,410 --> 00:03:47,240
- Hmm?
- Huh?

99
00:03:47,950 --> 00:03:51,990
♪ O hie thee forth o'er golden mead ♪

100
00:03:51,990 --> 00:03:55,250
♪ Yon is the maypole set  ♪

101
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:58,660
♪ A ribbon to wind thy soul ♪

102
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:02,010
♪ And to bind love to thy breast ♪

103
00:04:02,010 --> 00:04:03,430
What the...

104
00:04:03,430 --> 00:04:05,090
Oh, pardon me there.

105
00:04:05,090 --> 00:04:07,100
Say, you folks ought to don your vegetables

106
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:08,680
and celebrate the harvest with us.

107
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:09,510
Uh...

108
00:04:09,510 --> 00:04:11,430
Oh! You're wearing costumes.

109
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:16,440
Well, sure. Pumpkins can't move on their own... can they?

110
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:18,360
Ha. No. Yeah, no.

111
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:21,110
Good thing I didn't take this off.

112
00:04:21,110 --> 00:04:23,860
You guys find this place as creepy as I do, right?

113
00:04:23,860 --> 00:04:26,450
So it's some kind of weird cult

114
00:04:26,450 --> 00:04:28,200
where they wear vegetable costumes

115
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,790
and dance around a big thing.

116
00:04:29,790 --> 00:04:31,540
They seem nice enough.

117
00:04:31,540 --> 00:04:33,540
Okay, you're in denial. That's fine.

118
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:36,960
But I'm just saying, something feels off about this place.

119
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:40,020
Well,

120
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:43,300
maybe I can find someone here who will give us a ride home.

121
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:44,470
Greg, you stay out of trouble.

122
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:46,460
Beatrice, thank you, but you can leave.

123
00:04:47,010 --> 00:04:48,050
I can't leave.

124
00:04:48,050 --> 00:04:49,430
I'm honor-bound to help you

125
00:04:49,430 --> 00:04:50,720
since you guys helped me.

126
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:52,720
That's the bluebird rules.

127
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:54,430
Uh, okay.

128
00:04:54,430 --> 00:04:57,020
Beatrice, would you care for this dance?

129
00:04:57,020 --> 00:04:58,110
No thanks.

130
00:04:58,110 --> 00:05:00,070
No thanks, no thanks. I said no thank you.

131
00:05:04,290 --> 00:05:07,310
Say, aren't you a little too... early?

132
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:08,110
What do you mean?

133
00:05:08,110 --> 00:05:11,250
I mean it doesn't seem like you're ready to join us just yet.

134
00:05:11,290 --> 00:05:14,500
Join you? Yeah, no, I'm just passing through.

135
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:18,000
Folks don't tend to "pass through" Pottsfield.

136
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Oh... Yeah?

137
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Yeah. It's nice here.

138
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,380
Um, I'm really just looking t-to leave here as fast as possible.

139
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:27,410
Eh, what, what? Leave Pottsfield?

140
00:05:27,410 --> 00:05:28,970
Who wants to leave Pottsfield?!

141
00:05:28,970 --> 00:05:31,810
- What?
- He wants to leave Pottsfield.

142
00:05:31,810 --> 00:05:33,390
Oh, are we leaving already?

143
00:05:33,390 --> 00:05:34,730
Let's leave immediately.

144
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:37,400
I'm just trying to get home.

145
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:40,400
- They're not supposed to be here.
- Maybe he's here to steal our crops.

146
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,400
To ruin our party.

147
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:43,650
Or take off our pumpkin shoes!

148
00:05:43,650 --> 00:05:45,650
Uh, no, I, uh...

149
00:05:45,650 --> 00:05:48,410
Now, hold on, everybody.

150
00:05:48,410 --> 00:05:50,990
Let's not jump to any conclusions.

151
00:05:50,990 --> 00:05:52,080
Whoa.

152
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:54,330
Enoch, what shall we do with them?

153
00:05:54,330 --> 00:05:55,910
I-I'm done.

154
00:05:55,910 --> 00:05:57,920
Now, let's see here, boys.

155
00:05:57,920 --> 00:06:01,500
How did you end up in this little town of ours?

156
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:04,280
Well, we were trying to get home.

157
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:06,420
We came into town from the woods.

158
00:06:06,420 --> 00:06:10,200
Uh, we saw your farms and your houses and thought,

159
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:13,430
"hey, here's a normal place with normal people."

160
00:06:13,430 --> 00:06:15,430
And we both stepped on pumpkins.

161
00:06:15,430 --> 00:06:18,350
Yeah, a-and then we heard the music from the barn, and,

162
00:06:18,350 --> 00:06:20,350
well, uh...

163
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:21,610
h-how about we just leave?

164
00:06:21,610 --> 00:06:23,690
Now, let me get this straight...

165
00:06:23,690 --> 00:06:25,030
You come to our town,

166
00:06:25,030 --> 00:06:26,530
you trample our crops,

167
00:06:26,530 --> 00:06:29,440
you interrupt our private engagement,

168
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:31,200
and now you want to leave?

169
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:32,370
Uh...

170
00:06:32,370 --> 00:06:33,200
Yes.

171
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:35,950
You'll never convict!
You have no proof!

172
00:06:35,950 --> 00:06:37,540
This one's trying to escape!

173
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:38,540
Let me go!

174
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:39,870
I don't know these clowns!

175
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:41,580
Children, it saddens me that

176
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:44,960
you don't wish to stay here with us,

177
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:48,880
I simply have to punish you for your transgressions.

178
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:51,140
I told you this place was bad news.

179
00:06:51,140 --> 00:06:55,840
So, by order of the Pottsfield chamber of commerce,

180
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:57,920
I find you guilty of trespassing,

181
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:00,810
destruction of property, disturbing the peace,

182
00:07:00,810 --> 00:07:02,650
and murder.

183
00:07:02,650 --> 00:07:03,650
Murder?

184
00:07:03,650 --> 00:07:05,650
Oh, no, not murder.

185
00:07:05,650 --> 00:07:10,240
But for those other crimes, I sentence you to...

186
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:12,660
a few hours of manual labor.

187
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:14,330
Wait. What? Really?

188
00:07:14,330 --> 00:07:15,580
That's it?

189
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:19,160
♪ Among the fields of straw and stover ♪

190
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:24,880
♪ Clocked in 'till the work day is over ♪

191
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:30,970
♪ Time's a gentle stream, longer than it seems ♪

192
00:07:30,970 --> 00:07:34,510
♪ Patient is the night ♪

193
00:07:35,970 --> 00:07:40,640
♪ How I long to see her face now ♪

194
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:45,150
♪ Her starry, moonlit gaze now ♪

195
00:07:45,150 --> 00:07:50,490
♪ I know she's never late, so anxiously I wait ♪

196
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:54,740
♪ Patient is the night ♪

197
00:07:57,990 --> 00:08:00,040
Just a few hours of manual labor,

198
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:01,460
and we're almost done.

199
00:08:01,460 --> 00:08:03,460
And then what are you gonna do...

200
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:05,990
just wander around? This way and that way?

201
00:08:05,990 --> 00:08:08,050
Through the woods forevermore?

202
00:08:08,050 --> 00:08:09,560
Uh, uh,

203
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:12,050
maybe we'll just stay here in Pottsfield.

204
00:08:12,050 --> 00:08:13,300
It's nice here.

205
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:15,300
I don't know. I don't know.

206
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:17,680
Why do they even have you digging these holes?

207
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:19,810
Planting seeds or something.

208
00:08:19,810 --> 00:08:22,480
Huh, maybe they're gonna bury you out here.

209
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:23,480
pfft

210
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:25,150
Hey! Buried treasure!

211
00:08:25,150 --> 00:08:26,270
Whoa! Really?

212
00:08:26,270 --> 00:08:28,570
See, Beatrice? What'd you find?

213
00:08:28,610 --> 00:08:29,900
A skeleton!

214
00:08:31,650 --> 00:08:33,650
We're digging our own...

215
00:08:33,650 --> 00:08:34,410
Huh!

216
00:08:34,410 --> 00:08:36,990
I-I-I was wrong. I was wrong all along.

217
00:08:36,990 --> 00:08:38,280
I-I don't know how to get us home.

218
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:40,200
Use your little feet to pick our locks!

219
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:42,460
O-ho! Now you want my help?

220
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:44,460
I don't want your help.

221
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:48,210
Yes! I want your help!

222
00:08:48,210 --> 00:08:50,380
- Beatrice, serio...
- Your time is up!

223
00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:51,380
Aah!

224
00:08:55,430 --> 00:08:57,010
Have the holes been dug?

225
00:08:57,010 --> 00:08:58,350
Uh... Yeah.

226
00:08:58,350 --> 00:08:59,350
Splendid! Well then..

227
00:08:59,350 --> 00:09:00,260
But, no.

228
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:01,270
No?

229
00:09:01,270 --> 00:09:02,270
Uh...

230
00:09:02,270 --> 00:09:03,430
Psst!

231
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:05,690
Keep stalling.

232
00:09:05,690 --> 00:09:07,900
Right.
Yeah, uh, you know,

233
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:10,610
we were digging, and there were too many rocks.

234
00:09:10,610 --> 00:09:12,610
You guys don't like rocks, right?

235
00:09:12,610 --> 00:09:15,450
- I don't think we do.
- I don't think so.

236
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:15,450
No, we don't like rocks.

237
00:09:15,450 --> 00:09:17,200
See? So we were like,

238
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,910
"we should get rid of these rocks."

239
00:09:18,910 --> 00:09:20,080
Well, that's a good idea.

240
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,330
Right? Yeah.

241
00:09:21,330 --> 00:09:24,080
So, we were getting rid of the rocks and... huh?

242
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:24,750
Huh?

243
00:09:24,750 --> 00:09:26,670
What? They left me.

244
00:09:26,670 --> 00:09:28,510
So, what happened to the rocks?

245
00:09:28,510 --> 00:09:29,840
Uh, the rocks...

246
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:32,840
Yeah, they... they were, um, you know...

247
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:36,840
they... they... they got in the way of all the...

248
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:41,010
well, the dirt, you know, and... W-Whoa! Ohh!

249
00:09:41,010 --> 00:09:43,680
Welcome back, Larry!

250
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:43,680
Hey, he looks exactly the same.

251
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,930
What in the...

252
00:09:44,930 --> 00:09:47,330
Whooooop! Ooh!

253
00:09:49,110 --> 00:09:50,940
Yeah, Larry! Whoo!

254
00:09:49,110 --> 00:09:50,940
Look at that guy go!

255
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:54,650
Edward, this one's for you!

256
00:09:54,650 --> 00:09:57,490
They're all skeletons.

257
00:09:57,490 --> 00:10:00,160
Thanks for digging up the life of the party.

258
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:04,500
What a wonderful harvest. And what about you?

259
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:06,000
You sure you want to leave?

260
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,160
Me? Yes?

261
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:10,580
Oh, well. You'll join us someday.

262
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:11,590
Uh...

263
00:10:11,590 --> 00:10:12,470
Psst!

264
00:10:12,470 --> 00:10:13,790
Why are you still here?

265
00:10:13,790 --> 00:10:15,960
What do you mean? You guys left me!

266
00:10:17,590 --> 00:10:18,930
- Oh.
- Come on.

267
00:10:20,930 --> 00:10:22,930
Oh. Are they chasing us?

268
00:10:22,930 --> 00:10:23,930
- Nope.
- No.

269
00:10:24,930 --> 00:10:26,600
I-I thought you guys...

270
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:27,850
You're welcome.

271
00:10:28,850 --> 00:10:30,270
Thank you.

272
00:10:30,270 --> 00:10:31,640
I guess we're even now, huh?

273
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:33,690
You're not honor-bound to help us anymore.

274
00:10:33,690 --> 00:10:34,970
huh, I wish.

275
00:10:34,970 --> 00:10:37,780
But you weren't actually in any danger with those weirdos.

276
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:39,000
Oh, yeah!

277
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,240
Then you still have to help us get home.

278
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:41,950
I got it!

279
00:10:41,950 --> 00:10:45,700
I wish Wirt Jr. had fingernails so he could play the guitar better.

280
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:49,970
So... Yeah, I'll bring you to Adelaide.

281
00:10:49,970 --> 00:10:51,540
I mean, that's where I'm going anyway.

282
00:10:51,540 --> 00:10:53,290
Why are you going to Adelaide's

283
00:10:53,290 --> 00:10:54,550
I guess, in some ways,

284
00:10:54,550 --> 00:10:56,080
I'm trying to get home, too.

285
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,800
That's vague. What does that mean?

286
00:10:57,800 --> 00:10:59,550
I don't have to tell you anything.

287
00:10:59,550 --> 00:11:00,550
Well, I sure hope

288
00:11:00,550 --> 00:11:02,890
Adelaide is more helpful than that woodsman was.

289
00:11:02,890 --> 00:11:04,890
I think his directions were...

290
00:11:04,890 --> 00:11:06,060
not very good.
